{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/512977-pimp-my-durance","id":512977,"title":"Pimp my Durance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-13T09:23:21-07:00","id":512977,"title":"Pimp my Durance","content":"So, I have a Changeling concept for a game I need to actually shut up and finish. I have nearly everything planned out except one part, his Durance. The character was the childhood friend of another PC who was taken by the Fae. My character was the only one who noticed his friend was replaced with a fetch, and none of the grownups would believe him. He found clues (probably planted) to her whereabouts and a Fae / Huntsman / Whatever lured him into the Hedge to go find her. He wandered into the same Keeper's Realm.<br /> <br /> The Realm is a glorious shining city on the hill surrounded by infinite darkness on all sides. The Keeper is all about taking things from the mortal realm that remind Him of Himself and then turning them to reflect His glory even more. My character never made it to the actual shining city, instead only going so far as the infinite fields of broken glass (the corpses of everything that failed to reflect him properly) and darkness--the boundary that defined everything that was <i>not </i>the Keeper. After a while he finds a momento from his home and decides enough is enough. He turns his back on the girl he came to save and he goes home.<br /> <br /> How well this syncs up to 2e Darklings is amazing, and he's totally going to be a Darkling anyways but is pure coincidence. In response to 2e Darklings I think I'm going to make the &quot;momento&quot; be another Changeling that abandoned him to keep in line with that. The game will eventually update to 2e.<br /> <br /> But yeah, my dilemma is: what was life like in the field of infinite darkness and broken glass. What did he actually <i>do / what happened to him </i>and what kith(s) would naturally result? &quot;He walks in the field, and eventually turns around and just leaves&quot; is pretty boring. The character eventually goes on to deal heavily with Goblins / Market, and is a talented Oneirophysic.<br /> <br /> Will probably end up using this picture for the character's Mein (Arsham has some nice broken glass sculptures, definitely worth checking out)<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://barbourdesign.files.wordpress.com/2013/01/arsham-01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://barbourdesign.files.wordpress.com/2013/01/arsham-01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://barbourdesign.files.wordpress.com/2013/01/arsham-01.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://barbourdesign.files.wordpress.com/2013/01/arsham-01.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 05-13-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T07:18:44-07:00","id":514094,"title":"","content":"Just off the top of my head: <br /> <br /> The glass shards cutting him up, letting in the darkness, eventually too much gets in and he can't go on and has to turn back.<br /> As his eyes adjust to the darkness, the brightness gets to be too much and he can't go on.<br /> The negative reflections in the shards start to creep out, scream at him, scare the crap out of him.<br /> The shards are how the Hedge manifests right there, so he never actually made it to Arcadia, just got torn apart by the Hedge.<br /> <br /> See what you can do with some of those ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:20:22-07:00","id":514129,"title":"","content":"Of course it is entirely up to you, but I'm not sure I would like playing a character that didn't have a Keeper in some form. The fear that your Keeper is always looking for you is one of the main reasons to join a Court and provides much of the drama in a game of Changeling. Also, I always run my games as the Keeper being a manifestation of their Realm in Arcadia (or vice-versa), so having a mortal roaming around going unnoticed would not happen. I don't think it is unreasonable to have a &quot;shadow&quot; Keeper - they know you're there roaming around the fields of glass, and they are subtly shaping you in the way they shape all the other lost.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Keeper views you as the &quot;weak&quot; part of himself that he won't let enter his shining kingdom- doomed to live among the wasted and rejected. You are groomed more and more for this as your Keeper builds mazes of the glass that you have to crawl through and over, slicing your body with every move until you couldn't stand the pain anymore and you flee as a Darkling. There are a number of Kits that could work well, especially in 2e where they are less limited by Seeming choice. To name a few:<br /> <br /> - Skitterskulk: climbing and winding through the labyrinth of glass turned you into a creepy crawly<br /> - Chimera: walking through the discarded remnants of other Changlings you decide that to survive you need to become stronger and you work with what you have, cobbling together a kith from the shattered parts around you<br /> - Gravewight: dealing with the dead, fairly obvious<br /> - Mirrorskin: when your Keeper gazed out at the fields (Eye of Sauron style, or course) you needed to blend in somehow...<br /> - Bright One: the reflections of the mirrors. This would actually be an amazing dichotomy to have a Darkling Bright One. I picture a dark figure with like shining eyes or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5202-hotchepsoot","name":"HotChepSoot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T21:29:04-07:00","id":515814,"title":"","content":"If you want to take the instant karma route, you could have the friend he went to rescue become the very Huntsman sent out to retrieve him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Ideas:<br /> <br /> <br /> -Levinquick: Forced to crawl through broken glass, your nerves flared with jolts of pain. Unwilling to spend anymore time there, you scampered as quick as possible for the exit.<br /> <br /> <br /> -Lurker: You came there to retrieve somebody and hopefully not be caught in the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -Brollachan: You weren't worthy to become part of the Keeper's magnificence. Cast into the infinite void of darkness and surrounded by shards of broken glass on all sides, you experienced a terror you never thought possible. And that experience left you with a few ideas of how to get back at those you hold a grudge with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-16-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T08:06:31-07:00","id":521894,"title":"","content":"Well, your character is lost in a desert of glass, with only corpses for company, besides the Others (skittering things that hover on the edge of vision). So you take up a shard, even as it cuts your own hand, and start butchering the dead, skinning them to make your first shoes, your warming cloak. You make tools of bone and partake of the rotting flesh-- at times fighting the Others for the freshest leavings.<br /> <br /> <b>Gravewight</b>-- eater of the dead, ghost whisperer<br /> <b>Razorhand</b>-- this is normally not one of my favorites, but I like the idea that the fae glass becomes embedded in the character's hand and becomes part of him. If the player was open to non-darkling seemings, I might recommend <b>Gristlegrinder </b>with mouth of glass teeth or <b>Render</b>.<br /> <br /> I also would offer the idea that the desert of glass might be only one part of durance, and that it was one test of many to learn to survive. Then I would offer <b>Wizend Artist</b> as a possibility. How do you form a changeling that can forge moonlight into a sword? You strand him/her in more barren and life-threating environments until s/he can make something out of nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:01:46-07:00","id":598593,"title":"","content":"Mrah. So this concept died and is now rising again. Taking another crack at it. I'm focusing down the concept and toning down the Goblin Market aspects drastically. Going to be playing on Oneirophysic that goes around as a Pop Psychoanalyst. In terms of his relationship with mortals, he's a bit of a Dream Voyeur that rides dreams like Dr. House pops Vicodin. When he came back, it was some thirty years later and his fetch had a wife, kids, successful job, etc. Truly his fetch lived the american dream, and the character, Dr. Price, is jealous. He has a subconscious drive to one up his perception of his fetch's better life by having a <i>better</i> house a <i>better</i> family and a <i>better</i> job. He's willing to cheat and use magic to get it, which results in all sorts of shenanigans. In order to justify his voyeur habit, he is a bit of a philanthropist and when he invades people's dreams, he tries to use his talents to make their lives better. In terms of Changelings, he's an Oneirophysic that's a little too friendly with the local Goblins and is looked at unfavorably because of that.<br /> <br /> Back to the Durance. I'm jumping into an existing game by sharing a Keeper with another PC. They lived in the Shining City, my character was in the Eternal Darkness. We decided it'd be cool if her character <i>looked</i> very similar to the Keeper while my character <i>sounded</i> exactly like the Keeper. Keeping with that theme as well as the whole idea that Changelings tend to reclaim what happened to them I'm thinking the character was part of the whole process of making things more like his Keeper. When something in the realm became unacceptable--a Changeling was getting rebellious, the Keeper simply got bored of something, or something tried so hard to be the Keeper that it broke under the impossibility and/or cruelty, etc. it would be cast into the Darkness. There creatures (including my character) would try and &quot;fix&quot; them and re-indoctrinate them into understanding how awesome the Keeper was. Successes were either sent back or kept to work in the Fields. Failures were traditionally ground into glass. The workers were generally promised that if they did a good enough job they could get to see the Keeper in the Shining City, but it basically never happened.<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking the character found his way into the Darkness surrounding the Shining City and then wound up being mistaken as something that needed to be &quot;fixed&quot; (a common occurrence for anyone not personally escorted). He was indoctrinated and forced to work in the Fields. Many a fleeing Changeling fell under his knife, though he'd sometimes trade small mercies for stories from the Shining City.<br /> <br /> Eventually some scrappy, rebellious Changeling came through the process not once, not twice, but three times. This was completely unheard of, and my character wound up hiding her (largely becacuse &quot;wtf is this? I must understand.&quot;). Through that brief encounter she reminded him of home, why he came there, and challenged his loyalty. Originally she offered to take him with her. When the opportunity came, he hesitated because he couldn't leave the girl in the Shining City. His accomplice left him. A short while later, unwilling to continue doing what he was doing after his eyes were opened and unable to reach the city, he turned his back on the girl from his childhood and made his own journey.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 07-21-2015, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}